  "producer_and_algorithm_review": [
    "Mixed root reordering and parameter/kind changes previously reused stale operations. Pure reorder is now selected only with unchanged chunks and surface-dependent descriptors; a complete operation permutation is prepared before mutation.",
    "Root reordering previously discarded fragment ownership, forcing later removal to recompile unrelated subtrees. The selected permutation now updates existing ranges and command locations while preserving subtree and draw storage.",
    "Middle root insertion previously appended its authoritative command out of painter order. Command and execution order now move together and affected suffix locations are refreshed.",
    "Removing missing-plan substitutes exposed a real producer flaw: command reconstruction after painter compilation cleared the plan while leaving plan_compiled_during_update true. Structural commands are now finalized before plan/painter compilation, and any late flat-command rebuild clears that flag.",
    "Root fragment indexing now follows actual root command scope, including layers flattened through Groups. Inserted plain draws cannot cross the next command-scope layer, and a following multibatch Scene chooses structural compilation before mutation.",
    "Proven missing-plan, invalid root-range, duplicate parent-list and second command-identity-map retry paths are removed. Root mutation methods now return unit; actual fused/offscreen shape eligibility, nested ancestry and replacement-shape checks remain because they select different valid execution structures.",
    "Five CPU contracts and five Metal regressions cover 64 pairs of eight layer kinds, immutable prior plans, published plan presence, unchanged draw-storage sharing, mixed updates, grouped clips, multibatch Scene boundaries and later full compilation/removal. GPU regressions compare 20 outputs with fresh renderers and include independent analytic pixel checks.",
    "The aggregate insertion diagnostic was replaced by three focused permanent regressions. A missing import in an initial focused build was corrected before running its tests; that compiler error is not counted as a semantic regression.",
    "Final review found no remaining specific likely bug within the changed root-edit contracts. Flat command synchronization and nested offscreen eligibility still need broader producer/caller tracing; platform runtime work remains separate."
  ],
